    {
      "@id": "docs/platform.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "(top of file)",
      "prov:value": "<!--\n  AUTHORED, and flat under `docs/` like every other authored page here. It\n  lived at `/cat-harness/` until 2026-09-21, as the one authored file in a\n  namespace whose every other route is a generator's output at\n  `<handler>/<kind>/`. The owner settled that collision — THE HANDLER WINS\n  (bean `8h42`) — so the namespace is generated material only, and this page\n  moved out.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 8h42",
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/platform.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "(top of file)",
      "prov:value": "  Moving it also ends the two-pages-one-stem collision rather than containing\n  it: `docs/index.md` and `docs/cat-harness/index.md` shared the stem `index`,\n  and `resolvePoSources` finding a block-level PO by bare stem wrote five\n  locales of \"translation-coverage: fail, 2%\" about a page nobody had ever\n  translated (PR #691). That was contained by making a PO claim its subject\n  through its own gettext `#:` references. Now there is one `index`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#691"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/platform.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "(top of file)",
      "prov:value": "  This page is the one a person writes, and bean `06e3` §2 is why it exists at\n  all: an index says what there is, and nothing else. What a process is FOR,\n  when you would be in it, and what it is not, has to be written by somebody.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 06e3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/platform.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "(top of file)",
      "prov:value": "  TWO RULES THIS PAGE IS UNDER, both from `06e3`:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/platform.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "(top of file)",
      "prov:value": "  `nav_exclude` is deliberate: the left-hand navbar's structure is bean `603s`,\n  in flight in another session, and a nav entry added here would collide with\n  the section model it is building. So REACHABILITY COMES FROM A LINK instead\n  — the Home page points here. Measured 2026-09-21, before that link existed:\n  no page in this site linked to this one, and the comment here claimed it was\n  \"reachable by its route and from the links that point at it\". Zero links is\n  not \"the links that point at it\", and a page reachable only by typing its\n  URL is a page nobody reads.\n-->",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 603s",
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/platform.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "What the handler publishes, and why it is not here",
      "prov:value": "This page used to sit at `/cat-harness/` as the one authored file among them.\nTwo path rules meet there: `<base>/<handler>/<kind>/` is the machinery\nrendering something, and `<base>/<instance>/` is an instance presenting\nitself. The platform is both, so the rules collided at exactly that path, and\nthe owner settled it on 2026-09-21 — **the handler wins**. Bean `8h42`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/platform.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "What the handler publishes, and why it is not here",
      "prov:value": "The table is the four that exist, read from the sibling directories rather\nthan remembered — it named three for a day after the fourth landed."
    }
  ]
}
